# Where the wallet frame is served. Unset = same origin (local dev only, NOT isolated).
# Production: a separate origin, e.g. https://wallet.example.com
# These two variables must be set TOGETHER in production: with NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_ORIGIN
# set and NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_APP_ORIGIN unset, the frame's frame-ancestors falls back to
# 'self' and the app cannot embed it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_ORIGIN=
# Comma-separated app origins the frame answers. Unset = own origin.
# Production: e.g. https://app.example.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_APP_ORIGIN=

# --- The model gateway -------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel AI Gateway key, read by the `ai` package itself. On Vercel, leave this
# unset and the deployment's OIDC token is used instead. Without either, /api/models
# lists every model as unavailable and the chat cannot answer.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# OpenAI key, server only. When set, the `openai/*` models (the default, GPT-5.5) are called directly at OpenAI
# instead of through the gateway. Prices still come from the gateway's public model listing.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- The request reader (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# TypeSafe API key. Server only: never give it a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name. When set, the text of the person's
# latest message (nothing else: no address, no history, no balances) is sent to TypeSafe's Jev model to
# read what they asked for. The reading runs BESIDE the chat model, not in front of it: a market ranking
# is shown first only when the reading is confident and the model has not yet said anything.
# It changes what such a turn costs. A turn the reading acts on starts two model calls and is billed for
# the one it gives up on as well as the one it keeps, so it costs about one and a half times an ordinary
# turn. Every other turn costs exactly what it costs without this key. Any failure, or leaving this
# unset, means the chat works exactly as it does without it.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# --- The database ------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres connection string (Neon in production). Unset outside production = an
# embedded PGlite database under .data/pglite, so a fresh checkout needs no account.
# A production build with this unset refuses to start the database.
DATABASE_URL=
# Where the embedded database lives when DATABASE_URL is unset.
# PGLITE_DIR=.data/pglite

# --- Billing -----------------------------------------------------------------
# What is charged on top of the gateway's price, in basis points. 3000 = 30%.
BILLING_MARGIN_BPS=3000
# The smallest hold placed before a model call, in micro-USD. 10000 = $0.01.
BILLING_MIN_HOLD_MICROUSD=10000
# Adding credit with USDC (spec 14.3). OFF until the treasury AND at least one token address are set.
# A person sends USDC from their wallet to the treasury; the server credits only what it reads on the chain itself:
# a successful Transfer from the configured USDC contract, from the signed-in account, to the treasury.
# The address that receives deposits. Verify it before use: whoever holds its key holds the money.
BILLING_TREASURY_ADDRESS=
# The USDC contract on each payment network, as BILLING_USDC_<chainId>. Never guess one: take it from the
# issuer's documentation and check it (`cast code`, `cast call <address> "symbol()(string)"`). The server checks
# it too, and does not offer a network whose address has no code or does not call itself USDC.
# BILLING_USDC_5042002=
# A TESTNET network is ignored unless this is set to 1. Testnet USDC comes from a faucet, and the credit it buys
# is recorded as test credit but SPENDS LIKE ANY OTHER, on model calls you pay for. Set it only on a deployment
# where that is what you want (a demo with a capped gateway key, local development).
# BILLING_ALLOW_TESTNET_CREDIT=1
# How many blocks deep a deposit must be before it is credited. Default 12. A credit is not taken back if the
# chain later reorganises past this depth, so choose it for the network: more on a chain with slow finality.
# BILLING_CONFIRMATIONS=12
# The most one deposit is credited for, in micro-USD. Default 500000000 ($500). The page refuses a larger amount
# before it is sent; a larger deposit made some other way is received and NOT credited, and needs you.
# BILLING_MAX_PER_TOPUP_MICROUSD=500000000
#
# The app's own tokens (contracts/, e.g. EZT) are NOT configured here: an admin adds them on /admin with a fixed
# price per token. They are sent to the same BILLING_TREASURY_ADDRESS and need BILLING_ALLOW_TESTNET_CREDIT=1 on a
# testnet, like USDC.
#
# Specified but NOT built yet, so setting these does nothing: adding credit by card (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY,
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET) and a market-priced utility token (BILLING_TOKEN_ADDRESS). With no rail switched on, the
# out-of-credit card says so, and an operator adds credit with
#   pnpm --filter @repo/db credit:adjust <address> <usd> "<reason>"

# --- Server-side chain reads --------------------------------------------------
# The RPC endpoint the SERVER uses for a network, as RPC_URL_<chainId>, in place of the chain's public one.
# Public endpoints are shared and rate limited; a deployment that takes deposits should use its own.
# Must be https (or http to this machine). An endpoint that answers as a different chain is not used at all:
# that network is then not served until it is fixed, rather than quietly read from the public endpoint.
# RPC_URL_5042002=

# --- Funding from another chain (Aurora Intents) ------------------------------
# Server only: the key travels in the URL path of every call, so it must never reach a browser or a log.
# Without it, no network offers "from another chain". With it, only mainnets the service can deliver to do
# (see AURORA_BLOCKCHAIN in apps/web/lib/server/funding/aurora.ts); the testnets never do.
AURORA_INTENTS_API_KEY=

# --- Verified protocols (MCP) --------------------------------------------------
# Which protocols are trusted is decided at build time (packages/protocols/src/registry/verified.ts).
# These only say where a trusted protocol's server is. <ID> is the manifest id, upper-cased, dashes as
# underscores. With no URL set, that protocol is not offered. The key never reaches a browser.
# MCP_<ID>_URL=https://mcp.example.com/mcp
# MCP_<ID>_KEY=

# --- Scheduled jobs ------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables GET /api/cron/release-holds, which a scheduler calls with "Authorization: Bearer <this>" to release
# credit held by requests that never finished. Unset: the route answers 404. (Each account's own stale holds
# are also released when it next sends a message, so this is for accounts that have not come back.)
CRON_SECRET=

# --- Local development only -------------------------------------------------
# DEV_FREE_CREDIT=1: chat with the REAL model without worrying about credit. The signed-in account is topped back up
# to $100 of test credit whenever it falls below $10. Ignored in a production build, on Vercel, and whenever
# DATABASE_URL is set, so it can never touch a real ledger.
# DEV_FREE_CREDIT=1

# --- Tests only --------------------------------------------------------------
# Playwright sets E2E_TEST_HOOKS=1 on its own dev server: a scripted model, a test
# credit route and looser rate limits. It has no effect in a production build.

# --- Admin ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wallet addresses that may open /admin, comma separated. Unset: nobody can.
ADMIN_ADDRESSES=
